### §7.3 Interface

```
SealSensor.on_seal(goal_id: GoalId) -> None
GoalArtifactResolver.resolve(goal_id) -> ArtifactSet{t1, t2?, t3[], t4_row}
SourceSelector.select(ArtifactSet) -> SourcePlan          # C1 enforced here
FacetExtractor.extract(SourcePlan, NodeType) -> [FacetDraft]
EnvelopeBinder.bind(FacetDraft) -> NodeDraft              # status=candidate, no confidence
CompletenessGate.score(NodeDraft) -> (NodeDraft, Cell{E|P|A}[])
OutboxWriter.append(Bundle) -> BundleRef                  # append-only; no update/delete
```

`CompletenessGate` mirrors B0.1's `LedgerStore` lesson (§5.3's Pattern):
**no update or delete method exists**, so append-only is enforced by the shape of
the interface rather than by discipline.

### §7.4 State machines

**Node lifecycle (§4.2).** Emission enters at `candidate` only.

```
     (emission, §6.1b r4)
              │
              ▼
        ┌───────────┐  evidence binding (§4.2, ×5)   ┌───────────┐
        │ candidate │ ──────────────────────────────▶│ canonical │
        └─────┬─────┘   NEVER a frequency threshold  └─────┬─────┘
              │                                             │
              │ falsifier observed          supersedes edge  │
              ▼                                             ▼
        ┌───────────┐                                ┌─────────────┐
        │  refuted  │◀───── falsifier observed ──────│ superseded  │
        └───────────┘                                └─────────────┘
        retained, never deleted (FPL-2, ✓1, ✓4)
```

**Probe consequence:** with `falsifier` absent on 100% of extracted nodes
(§5.1), the `→ refuted` transition is **unreachable for every node S1 emits
today**. Truth Maintenance has no trigger. This does not block S1 — it means C2
is a precondition for S3, not an optional polish.

**Extraction cell.** `absent → partial → extractable` is monotone; the
`CompletenessGate` may never promote a cell by inference. A cell that would
require fabrication is emitted as an explicit null with a reason, never omitted
silently — the same discipline §5.1 (A5) mandates for projections: **omission
must be visible.**

